# Symphony client

Repository: [[repo_slug | to_json]]. Default branch: [[default_branch | to_json]].
Linear team: [[linear_team_key | to_json]]. Each issue supplies its project.

Read README, AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md when present. Use `.symphony.cfg.json`
build/test arrays; preserve setup, lint and application CI. Validate locally,
use Docker for environment gaps, then require published-head CI. Empty required
checks are **unconfigured**; record observed names/workflows/App IDs before
activation. Keep the Cadence advisory check outside required checks.

Omit optional `symphony-client-ci.yml` when application CI covers the commands;
otherwise align its arrays with config and supply application setup. Reviewed
shared code runs the exact PR head with no named secrets. Wakeups use trusted
helpers and default-branch config, passing only `CADENCE_LINEAR_API_TOKEN`.

Select `ci.mode` during onboarding without changing the eight Copier answers:

- `native` (or omission): use installed tools. Passing local checks skip Docker;
  missing tools/services may use the client's documented container as fallback.
- `docker`: supply the application's Dockerfile and explicit setup/build/test
  arrays to build and run it. The field does not wrap commands automatically.
  Mount only the issue workspace, use its UID/GID, remove task containers and
  record image digest/results. No generic Dockerfile is supplied.
- `remote`: run available checks, record gaps, fix failures and publish for
  mandatory current-head CI. Unrun checks are not passes; no host/Docker setup.

Every mode needs a working GitHub CI toolchain. Pending/missing CI uses Unhappy
with `wake:15m`; failures return nonterminal issues to Active, passing CI to Inactive.
Preserve terminal/head guards. Live mode/bridge proof remains CT-A.

Review event/manual, handoff and cleanup callers share a reviewed workflow/helper
revision and explicit named secrets. Ingress is secret-free. Follow review context
for provider selection; report live execution separately from generated files.

Run the [PR guidance](docs/engineering/symphony/pull-requests.md) fetch/render
commands on creation and every refresh; retain generated state colors and links.

## Merge conflict wakeups

`Symphony Client Wakeups` checks labeled, same-repository PRs on `pull_request_target`
and default-branch pushes (PRs targeting that branch). Recovery at minutes 7, 22,
37 and 52 UTC checks all open Symphony PRs, including other bases. Unknown mergeability
waits for recovery; schedules may be delayed or disabled after inactivity.

- Publish the accepted conflict bridge on workflow `alpha`, then install the caller
  on the default branch and enable Actions/schedules. Verify delivery after publication.
- Pass only `CADENCE_LINEAR_API_TOKEN`; its owner needs issue/team/project reads,
  Cadence-workpad writes and issue-state updates in the configured team. Record the
  authenticated owner; no particular account display name is required.
- Retain read permissions for contents/PRs/checks/statuses/Actions. No PR write key,
  App signing key or provider secret is needed. Execute fixed trusted shared helpers,
  read default-branch config and never execute PR code.
- Keep config team, PR title/branch ticket, project metadata and labels consistent.
  Ambiguous/mismatched associations fail closed; terminal issues and closed/merged
  PRs remain unchanged. Leave active workers alone for a later recovery check.

Confirmed conflicts wake waiting issues to Active (legacy Rework). The workpad and
Actions summary record identity, actor, PR/head/base, run URL, resolution instruction
and mutation/skip. A durable per-repository/PR-head receipt suppresses repeats across
history rotation/base advancement; a new head is eligible. CI defers conflicts here;
unknown mergeability uses Unhappy + `wake:15m` for the existing timer to recheck.
Symphony resolves conflicts. Live proof uses a disposable task-linked PR in Inactive:
advance its base with a conflict, retain the push/recovery run and Active readback,
then verify duplicate suppression at the unchanged head. Fixtures do not prove delivery.

## Client session skills

Load these skills from this generated client in the human-operated session:

- [Project factory](.agents/skills/symphony-project-factory/SKILL.md), retaining
  its `templates/` directory; invoke only when a human requests project setup.
- [Linear GraphQL](.agents/skills/linear-graphql/SKILL.md), retaining
  `agents/openai.yaml` and `scripts/linear-graphql.mjs`. Prefer injected
  `linear_graphql`; when absent in a human-operated factory session, use the
  authenticated script with the same identity/preflight/staging/readback guards.
  Auth failure stops dependent writes without switching identity or transport;
  hosted workers retain injected auth. Already-authorized writes need no extra confirmation.
- Load [Replan](scripts/symphony/runtime-bundle/skills/symphony-replan/SKILL.md) from
  its nested path with the [guide](docs/engineering/symphony/replanning.md) and factory templates.

Keep a separate [reviewed tooling checkout](https://github.com/1000lines/symphony-example/tree/fd383f5760a2ba62ea6f6295bd6dd21cc0cb9e9e)
with locked dependencies and the CT-C config reader; verify hosted `ci.mode` support
before enabling a mode. `SYMPHONY_TOOLING_ROOT` names this checkout for workflow,
color, DAG and proof/review guides; client plans and skill-relative resources stay local.
Record checkout refs/locations and loaded resources; target the client and its projects.

[CT-O's setup and invocation procedure](https://linear.app/1000lines/issue/100-54)
verifies initial/repeated/additional-project loading and replan's nested path.
Copying is not installation/execution; hosted workers do not install the factory.

## Review and App setup

Start with the [Cadence onboarding skill](.agents/skills/cadence-onboarding/SKILL.md)
for credential names/scopes, App grants, environment admission and readiness.
Its `Symphony Client Setup` probe checks repository/protected-job credentials,
without AI review. Verify installed jobs and a real review/check/Linear handoff
before claiming onboarding complete.

Author App: [[symphony_app_slug | to_json]]. Reviewer App: [[cadence_app_slug | to_json]].
Reviewer choice: [[cadence_reviewer | to_json]]; see [review context](.github/symphony/REVIEW.md).
Provision credentials separately from answers and commands. At runtime an OpenAI
key selects Codex (including when both keys exist), otherwise an Anthropic key
selects Claude. Neither key fails early; authentication failures never fall back.

Public MVP forks use the accepted existing Cadence App; installation does not
provide the named Actions secrets. Direct/private targets use the inert
[App manifest](.github/symphony/cadence-app-manifest.json) in the operator's
[GitHub manifest registration flow](https://docs.github.com/en/apps/sharing-github-apps/registering-a-github-app-from-a-manifest).
It requests repository read access and PR/issue/check write access, with no
webhook receiver or subscribed events; native GitHub Actions provide delivery.
Verify grants/IDs and provision through onboarding; rendering performs neither.

